{His pawn on g6 has two steps left, and his king on g5 is escorting it home. Saving the draw is all you can hope for.}
1... Kf8 {Kf8 stands in front of the pawn: the Philidor rule, king in front, and that single square is the whole defence. [%csl Gf8]} (1... Rg1+ {Checking first with Rg1+ just lets his king step around it and keep escorting the pawn.} 2. Kf6 Rf1+ 3. Kg7 {The pawn queens. Lost. The checks never touched the pawn's own road home.}) (1... Ke7 {Ke7 is one square out, and it is already too late to hold the draw from there.} 2. Kh6 Rh1+ 3. Kg7 {Lost. His king reaches g7 to guard the pawn, and it queens on the very next move.}) (1... Rf1 {Guarding the queening square from the side with Rf1 is not enough on its own.} 2. Kh6 Rh1+ 3. Kg7 {Lost. The check comes a move too late to keep his king off the square on g7.}) (1... Ra5+ {Ra5+ checks him right where his king wanted to go anyway, straight toward the corner.} 2. Kh6 Ra6 3. Kh7 {Lost. His king reaches the corner and shields the pawn all the way home.}) (1... Ra7 {The seventh row does not help against a pawn already on the sixth.} 2. Kh6 Kf8 3. Rd8+ {Lost. The check drives your king away, and the pawn queens right behind it.}) 2. g7+ {He pushes the pawn to g7 with check. Now help yourself to it right away.} 2... Kxg7 {The pawn is gone, and a rook alone against your rook can never mate you. Drawn. [%csl Gg7]} (2... Kf7 {Kf7 is also a draw: from there the pawn cannot run anywhere at all.} 3. Rd7+ Kg8 {You will eat the pawn on g7 next move, and the game is a clean draw.}) (2... Kg8 {Kg8 is also fine, and the pawn falls just the same either way.} 3. Rd8+ Kxg7 {Drawn. The check gains the move you need to scoop up the pawn all the same.}) (2... Ke7 {Stepping away from the pawn with Ke7 lets it run without any king to stop it.} 3. Kg6 {His king walks the pawn all the way home to queen. Lost.}) (2... Ke8 {Ke8 steps away from the pawn on g7 when it could simply be taken.} 3. g8=Q+ {Lost. A new queen is born with check, and your rook cannot hold a whole queen off.}) 0-1


