{A new word: the bridge, where your rook blocks his last check so your king can shelter behind it. First climb your king toward the pawn on f7. [%cal Yd5e6]}
1. Ke6 {Ke6 climbs a row closer to the pawn on f7, instead of retreating from the check. That is the whole idea of the climb. [%csl Ge6]} (1. Kd6 {Kd6 runs away from the checks, and it leaves your pawn to fend for itself.} 1... Kg7 2. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {The queen lives one move on f8 before his rook takes her straight back. Drawn.}) (1. Kc6 {Kc6 steps away from the pawn on f7, and his rook gets to f5 in time.} 1... Rf5 2. f8=Q Rxf8 {Drawn. His rook stops the new queen the moment she is born.}) (1. Kd4 {Kd4 goes backwards: the pawn cannot wait around for your king down there.} 1... Rf5 2. f8=Q Rxf8 {Drawn. Your king never reached the pawn, so his rook simply takes the new queen.}) (1. Kc4 {Kc4 is too far from everything that matters: neither the checks nor the pawn are in reach.} 1... Rf5 2. f8=Q Rxf8 {Drawn. His rook was always close enough to collect the new queen.}) 1... Ra6+ {He checks again. Keep climbing your king toward the pawn. [%cal Ye6e7]} 2. Ke7 {Two rows closer now, on e7, and your pawn on f7 is guarded at last. [%csl Ge7]} (2. Kf5 {Kf5 heads toward his rook, but it walks away from your own pawn.} 2... Kg7 3. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. His king reaches f8 in time to take the new queen the moment she appears.}) (2. Kd7 {Kd7 goes sideways, and the pawn is left on its own again.} 2... Kg7 3. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. Unescorted on f8, the new queen lasts only one single move.}) (2. Kd5 {Kd5 climbs back down toward the fifth row, and all the work you did is undone.} 2... Rf6 3. f8=Q Rxf8 {Drawn. His rook blocks the pawn's road and then eats the new queen.}) (2. Ke5 {Ke5 steps backwards again, and the climb has to start all over.} 2... Kg7 3. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. His king strolls over to f8 and simply takes the new queen there.}) 2... Ra7+ {Another check. Now step across, beside the pawn. [%cal Ye7f6]} 3. Kf6 {Kf6 stands beside the pawn, guarding it, and ready to build the bridge. [%csl Gf6]} (3. Kf8 {Kf8 also wins: you step out of the check instead of blocking it.} 3... Ra8+ {Still winning, but on f8 your king blocks the queening square, and his checks go on longer.}) (3. Ke6 {Ke6 also wins, though you have gone back a step from where you were.} 3... Ra6+ {Still winning, but you are back on e6 where you were one move ago.}) (3. Ke8 {Ke8 also wins, but your king keeps drifting away from the pawn.} 3... Ra8+ {Winning still, though e8 leaves your king two squares from f7 and in line for checks.}) (3. Kd6 {Kd6 is now too far from the pawn on f7 to help it queen safely.} 3... Kg7 4. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. His king gets to f8 first and takes the new queen straight away.}) (3. Kd8 {Kd8 goes back toward the corner and away from the pawn on f7.} 3... Kg7 4. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. Your king is a whole column from the action, and his simply takes the new queen.}) 3... Ra6+ {His last useful check. Block this one with the rook itself, on e6. [%cal Ye4e6]} 4. Re6 {The bridge! Your rook blocks the check, and the pawn walks straight home. Now watch it queen. [%csl Ge6][%cal Gf7f8][%tail]} (4. Ke7 {Ke7 also wins: you step out of the check instead of building the bridge.} 4... Ra7+ {It still wins, but his checks keep coming until your rook builds the bridge anyway.}) (4. Kg5 {Running from the check with Kg5 leaves the pawn without any escort.} 4... Kg7 5. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. Nobody is left to guard the new queen, and his king simply takes it.}) (4. Ke5 {Ke5 goes backwards, and the whole climb toward the pawn is wasted.} 4... Kg7 5. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. His king wanders back over to f8 and takes the new queen there.}) (4. Kf5 {Kf5 steps back to the fifth row, away from the pawn on f7.} 4... Kg7 5. f8=Q+ Kxf8 {Drawn. His king is right there on f5 to take the new queen the moment she appears.}) 4... Ra8 5. Rd6 5... Kh6 6. Rd1 6... Ra6+ 7. Ke7 7... Ra8 8. f8=Q+ {A new queen stands on f8, with check, and your king on e7 is guarding her. That is the bridge: your rook blocked the check on e6, and the pawn walked all the way home.} 1-0


