(2. Kc7 {Kc7 also wins: your king steps up beside the pawn to walk it in.} 2... Rh1 3. Rd2 {Still winning: your king shepherds the pawn home from right next to it.}) (2. Rd3 {Rd3 also wins: the rook drops back out of his king's reach and still owns the d column.} 2... Rb2+ {His checks start, but your rook on d3 keeps his king cut off and the pawn still runs. Winning.}) (2. Rd4 {Rd4 steps back as well, and that wins too.} 2... Rb2+ {Still winning: his king stays shut out on the e column while your king walks up.}) (2. Rd8 {Rd8 goes all the way back to the last row and still wins.} 2... Rb2+ {Winning: from d8 your rook also guards c8, the queening square. [%cal Gd8c8]}) (2. Rg7 {Rg7 swings the rook along the seventh row, away from his king, and still wins.} 2... Rb2+ {Still winning: your rook on g7 keeps his king off the seventh row.}) (2. Ra7 {Ra7 also wins, but it lets his king come back.} 2... Kd6 {His king returns to d6 in front of your pawn, and you have to push it away again. Still winning, just slower.}) (2. Rb7 {Rb7 wins too, though the rook leaves the d column.} 2... Kd6 {With his king back on d6, the pawn needs your rook's help once more. Winning, but longer.}) (2. Ka6 {Ka6 still wins, but it walks your king onto the a column.} 2... Ra2+ {Checks from a2 now drive your king around before it can help the pawn. Still a win.}) (2. Ka7 {Ka7 also wins, going round by the far corner.} 2... Ra2+ {His rook checks from a2, and your king has a longer road to c8. Still winning.}) (2. Ka5 {Ka5 steps backwards, though it still wins.} 2... Ra2+ {Your king has to climb back up through his checks. Winning, but slowly.}) (2. Kb5 {Kb5 steps back beside the pawn and still wins.} 2... Rc2 {His rook gets behind your pawn on c2, so the walk home is longer. Still winning.}) (2. Kc5 {Kc5 still wins, standing right next to the pawn.} 2... Rh1 {His rook waits on h1. Your king is next to the pawn but further from c8. Still a win.}) (2. Rc7 {Rc7 parks your own rook directly in front of your own pawn, blocking its road.} 2... Rb2+ 3. Ka5 Ra2+ {Drawn. The checks never stop, and the pawn can never get past your rook.}) 2... Rb2+ 3. Kc8 3... Ra2 4. Rd1 4... Ra8+ 5. Kb7 5... Ra2 6. Rb1 6... Rc2 7. c7 7... Kd7 8. Rd1+ 8... Ke7 9. c8=Q 9... Rxc8 10. Kxc8 {Your king takes on c8: his bare king against your rook, a win. [%csl Gc8]} 1-0


